xnu 0289: a photo of a panic names the failure site

The panel cannot be scrolled and a panic is longer than the screen, so the
first line - the reason - was gone by the time the dump finished. The console
is now a client of the early framebuffer's HUD rows: the reason's first line
and the panic's format string go on the two bottom rows, which nothing else
writes, and the formatted copy is printed at the top after the dump.

Two CPUs can panic at once (one assertion, one lock timeout on the lock the
first was holding) and the second report used to overwrite the first: only the
first report reaches the screen. The formatted message can itself fault when a
%s argument is the corrupt thing, so the format string - a constant in the
kernel image - is reported on its own path.

Data aborts report ESR/FAR/PC/LR/CPSR/x0 on labelled HUD rows before the
generic handler prints, and the ticket lock's verify panics carry the owner,
the caller and the CPU, so a "not owned" panic says which thread held it.
Secondaries mark the stage they reached in a 32x16 block at the bottom
straight from assembly, with the MMU off, because arm_init runs before the
console exists.

